+"""Workflow command for manual relevance review.
+
+Why a separate command
+----------------------
+Determining `relevance` for 332 candidates by hand cannot realistically be done by editing JSON directly
+(and fields are very easy to get wrong). This command does two things:
+
+    patentkit review export --with-abstract     # export an editable CSV worksheet
+    patentkit review apply review.csv --apply   # write the determinations back to JSON
+
+Design points
+-------------
+* **CSV rather than Markdown**: it must both open in Excel and be read back verbatim; only CSV round-trips reliably.
+* **`utf-8-sig`**: BOM required, otherwise Excel shows mojibake for Chinese.
+* **Determination columns are separate**: export is read-only and never touches existing values; apply only changes
+  rows whose "determination columns" are non-empty, and skips blank rows entirely — never resets un-judged entries to defaults.
+* **Only three fields are changed**: `relevance` / `role` / `novelty_check` (+ `review_note`).
+  All other fields are left untouched.
+* **Full abstracts**: the candidate's `summary_zh` is truncated to 190 characters;
+  here the **full abstract** is taken from the `raw/` artifact in preference (284 characters on average).
+
+The determination criteria are in the `relevance_levels` section of `00_methodology/glossary.yml`.
+**The threshold is ≥4**: G-S-02 counts only candidates with relevance≥4.
+"""
